      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1954, the Hoffman Clock Museum opened inside Newark Public Library, showcasing a unique collection of antique clocks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Newark is the birthplace of the Jackson & Perkins Company, founded in 1872 by Albert Jackson and his son-in-law Charles H. Perkins, a pioneer in rose cultivation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark%2C_New_York",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s historic Erie Canal locks, including Lock 28B, still welcome boaters and are part of the Port of Newark Interpretive Center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://newarknychamber.org/about-us/about-newark",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Jackson–Perkins House at 310 High Street, once the company’s headquarters, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Newark‑Arcadia Historical Society Museum, located a short walk from the canal, preserves local history and hosts rotating exhibitions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://newarknychamber.org/about-us/about-newark",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Newark was incorporated as a village in 1853, making it one of the oldest communities along the Erie Canal.",
